      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "name": "A title",
       "content": "Why I Rebuilt\nMy Portfolio",
       "x": 200,
       "y": 204,
       "fontFamily": "Syne",
       "fontWeight": "800",
       "fontSize": 52,
       "fill": "#F2F0E9",
       "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
       "textAlign": "left",
       "width": 700,
       "letterSpacing": -1.6,
       "lineHeight": 1.0,
       "id": "B1094"
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "name": "A excerpt",
       "content": "My old portfolio was a mess. Here is how I rebuilt it with Next.js 15,\nTailwind v4, and a feature-based architecture \u2014 and what I deleted\non the way.",
       "x": 200,
       "y": 322,
       "fontFamily": "Geist",
       "fontWeight": "400",
       "fontSize": 16.5,
       "fill": "#C9D0CA",
       "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
       "textAlign": "left",
       "width": 680,
       "lineHeight": 1.6,
       "id": "B1095"
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "name": "A byline",
       "content": "ADITYA HIMAWAN  /  06:12 READ  /  2026.04.15",
       "x": 200,
       "y": 404,
       "fontFamily": "Geist Mono",
       "fontWeight": "500",
       "fontSize": 8.5,
       "fill": "#6E7771",
       "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
       "textAlign": "left",
       "width": 680,
       "letterSpacing": 1.1,
       "id": "B1096"
      },
      {
       "type": "rectangle",
       "name": "A hair",
       "x": 200,
       "y": 430,
       "width": 760,
       "height": 1,
       "cornerRadius": 0,
       "fill": "#FFFFFF18",
       "id": "B1097"
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "name": "A p1",
       "content": "Last year I built my portfolio in a rush. It worked, but the codebase was not something I was proud of. I had 30 dead component files sitting in the repo, versioned names like hero-2025-v2.tsx that told a story of failed experiments I never cleaned up, and a single data.ts file that contained everything \u2014 projects, blog posts, social links, experience data, all jammed into one 200-line export.",
       "x": 200,
       "y": 454,
       "fontFamily": "Geist",
       "fontWeight": "400",
       "fontSize": 15.5,
       "fill": "#C9D0CA",
       "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
       "textAlign": "left",
       "width": 690,
       "lineHeight": 1.7,
       "id": "B1098"
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "name": "A h2 problem",
       "content": "The problem",
       "x": 200,
       "y": 608,
       "fontFamily": "Space Grotesk",
       "fontWeight": "600",
       "fontSize": 22,
       "fill": "#F2F0E9",
       "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
       "textAlign": "left",
       "width": 500,
       "letterSpacing": -0.2,
       "id": "B1099"
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "name": "A p2",
       "content": "The old structure was type-based. All components lived in one folder, all hooks in another, all utils in another. It sounds organized until you try to add a feature. Adding a new page meant touching four different folders \u2014 components, hooks, utils, and the route itself. Deleting a feature was worse. I had to hunt through the entire codebase to find every import, every reference, every leftover utility that only existed to support the thing I was removing.",
       "x": 200,
       "y": 648,
       "fontFamily": "Geist",
       "fontWeight": "400",
       "fontSize": 15.5,
       "fill": "#C9D0CA",
       "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
       "textAlign": "left",
       "width": 690,
       "lineHeight": 1.7,
       "id": "B1100"
      },
