       "id": "B1110"
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "name": "Quote",
       "content": "\u201cDeleting ruthlessly was the second most\nimportant thing. Dead code is not just clutter \u2014\nit is confusion.\u201d",
       "x": 224,
       "y": 1036,
       "fontFamily": "Syne",
       "fontWeight": "700",
       "fontSize": 24,
       "fill": "#F2F0E9",
       "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
       "textAlign": "left",
       "width": 680,
       "letterSpacing": -0.5,
       "lineHeight": 1.28,
       "id": "B1111"
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "name": "Quote cite",
       "content": "\u2014 WHY I REBUILT MY PORTFOLIO",
       "x": 224,
       "y": 1114,
       "fontFamily": "Geist Mono",
       "fontWeight": "500",
       "fontSize": 8,
       "fill": "#6E7771",
       "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
       "textAlign": "left",
       "width": 500,
       "letterSpacing": 1.2,
       "id": "B1112"
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "name": "A p3",
       "content": "The single biggest improvement was grouping by feature, not by type. Everything else \u2014 the dead file cleanup, the barrel exports, the better naming conventions \u2014 those were consequences of that one decision. When you structure code around what it does instead of what kind of file it is, the right organization follows naturally.",
       "x": 200,
       "y": 1152,
       "fontFamily": "Geist",
       "fontWeight": "400",
       "fontSize": 15.5,
       "fill": "#C9D0CA",
       "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
       "textAlign": "left",
       "width": 690,
       "lineHeight": 1.7,
       "id": "B1113"
      },
